  "source_transcript": "My crush jumped into my arms in a haunted forest. It was our school's test of courage, and I'd drawn her name. Stay close. I'm not scared of anything. A ghost dropped out of a tree, and she grabbed my arm. A skeleton sat up in the graveyard, and she hugged me so tight I couldn't breathe. A zombie crawled out of a grave, and she jumped straight into my arms. I didn't even blink. The ghosts weren't the problem. The problem was that she smelled like strawberries. Her face was an inch from mine, and my heart was louder than the screaming. Then something cold and wet touched my ankle. I screamed so loud the zombie ran away. It was a frog, a tiny one. I jumped into her arms, and she carried me out of the forest. My hero, the whole class was waiting at the exit. Our teacher looked confused. Where did you find ghosts? We canceled them. It rained. We turned around. At the edge of the trees, a ghost, a skeleton, and a zombie were clapping.",
